<article class="env-notation" id="0B4785">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B4785">Notation <span data-tag="0B4785">8.2.9.7</span>.</a>latching objectobject!latchingLsubJ@$L_{J}(X)$ Let $\calJ $ be a Reedy category, $\calC $ a category which admits small limits and colimits, and $X: \calJ \rightarrow \calC $ a functor. For every object $J \in \calJ $, we define the <em>latching object</em> $L_{J}(X)$ to be the colimit </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \varinjlim _{J' \in \calJ ^{R}_{/J}, J' \neq J} X(J'). \]
</div>
  <p> Similarly, we define the <em>matching object</em>matching objectobject!matching MsubJ@$M_{J}(X)$ to be the limit </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \varprojlim _{J' \in \calJ ^{L}_{J/}, J' \neq J} X(J'). \]
</div>
  <p> We then have canonical maps $L_{J}(X) \rightarrow X(J) \rightarrow M_{J}(X).$ </p>
</article>